From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: folia-linear-ci <folia-linear-ci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:42:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Linear shared flush pool + direct-into-image (minecraft-0016)

Loop-3 (agent 24): ONE shared bounded server-wide flush pool behind
flush-max-threads (NOT per-coordinator: 9 coordinators on 3-world server;
NOT ForkJoinPool: managed-blocker compensation breaks the memory budget;
NOT invokeAll: cancels tasks on interrupt, truncating a durability barrier;
NOT Moonrise's pool: submit-and-block from those threads deadlocks).
Caller participates as worker, joins before returning (durability barrier).
<=1 keeps the pre-patch serial loop byte-identical.

ALSO: doFlush decompresses each LZ4 slot straight into final offset in
image (removes one full region copy; previously held plain[] AND image ~2x).

